What this directory adds
- An append-only action journal (SHA-256 hash chain and a tip sidecar).
- Workspace checkpoints and rewind, plus a command seam for upstream QEMU
  savevm/loadvm and Lume stop-clone checkpoints. See docs/SNAPSHOTS.md.
- A YAML policy for forbidden actions and actions that need approval.
- An uncertainty gate: low confidence or low sample agreement escalates to a
  stronger model, or to a person when the action is dangerous and very unsure.
  The idea follows LEASH (https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.22280). This is not a
  reproduction of that paper's models or experiments.
- A six-task scripted comparison of a one-shot executor against this harness.
  Cua-Bench and OSWorld were not run.
- A demo journal, storyboard, and GIF of a mistaken delete that is rewound.
